# www/admin/ exists only to hold the admin's static assets. Without this,
# mod_dir sees the bare /admin route as a directory and 301s it to /admin/
# before the front-controller rewrite in ../.htaccess can claim it, costing a
# redirect hop on the admin's most-requested URL.
#
# Scoped to this directory on purpose: DirectorySlash stays ON everywhere else
# (mod_autoindex is loaded server-wide, and turning it off site-wide can expose
# directory listings).
DirectorySlash Off
Options -Indexes
